course: dictionary
lesson: 15512
title: Subordination
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Subordination means putting one thing under another. In grammar, a subordinate clause is a less important part of a sentence, joined to the main clause by a word such as because, although, when or if. «I went home because it was raining.» The main clause is «I went home», which makes sense on its own. «because it was raining» depends on it and cannot stand alone as a sentence.
explain: Look at «Although the sun was shining, we took umbrellas.» The word although starts the subordinate clause. Words like although, because, when and if are called subordinating conjunctions. They join the less important clause to the main one.
explain: Subordination also describes control and rank. A soldier is under the subordination of an officer, which means the officer has authority over the soldier. A subordinate worker depends on a boss in the same way that a subordinate clause depends on a main clause.
explain: To check a sentence, ask: can the main clause stand alone? If yes, the other part is the subordinate clause. Then ask which word joins them, because that will be a subordinating conjunction.
fact: Subordination means being under someone else's control or authority, or being placed in a lower, less important position.
fact: In grammar, subordination joins a less important clause to a main clause, making a complex sentence.
fact: Common subordinating conjunctions are because, although, when, if and while.
fact: «Because» starts a subordinate clause in «I stayed in because it was cold.»
fact: A subordinate clause cannot stand alone as a sentence, but the main clause can.
exercise: «I went home because it was raining.» Which word is the subordinating conjunction? | *because | raining | home | went
exercise: «We played outside when the sun came out.» Which part is the main clause? | outside | the sun came out | *We played outside | when the sun came out
exercise: Which word is a subordinating conjunction? | quickly | *if | happy | bright
test: «She smiled although she was tired.» Which part is the subordinate clause? | She | She smiled | *although she was tired | was tired
test: A pupil is under the subordination of a teacher. What does this mean? | The pupil is teaching the class | The pupil and the teacher are equals | The pupil is the teacher's boss | *The pupil is under the teacher's authority
exam: Which sentence contains a subordinate clause? | Birds sing. | The dog barked. | Run fast! | *The dog barked because a stranger knocked.
